shape theory.fractal.no-incoherent-embedding : theory.fractal.upward, theory.coherence.law0 {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 7.5 (No Incoherent Embedding).
// A coherent shape system cannot contain an incoherent emergent
// subsystem upon which its coherence depends. If a required
// subsystem is incoherent, the parent system is incoherent.
//
// Contrapositive: if a shape system persists, every subsystem whose
// contact it depends on coheres. Persistence at the top guarantees
// coherence all the way down through every contact shape the system's
// coherence requires.
//
// This is why coherence is fractal: it holds at every layer, not
// because it is imposed from any particular level, but because
// failure at any level propagates through contact shapes to all
// levels that depend on them.
//
// Derives from: theory.fractal.upward, theory.coherence.law0
  """
}
